  "ingredients": [
    "48 ounce bone-in chicken wings",
    "1 medium lemongrass",
    "3 teaspoon fresh garlic",
    "1/4 cup coconut vinegar",
    "2 tablespoon calamansi juice",
    "2 tablespoon water",
    "1 tablespoon low-carb brown sugar replacement",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "1/4 teaspoon black pepper",
    "1 tablespoon fresh ginger",
    "1/4 cup duck fat",
    "2 tablespoon annatto seeds"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Portion chicken wings into wingettes and drumettes, discard tips.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/chicken-inasal-filipino-chicken-bbq/#wprm-recipe-53235-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/chicken-inasal-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a food processor (or blender), add lemongrass, garlic, vinegar, calamansi juice, water, sweetener, salt, pepper, and ginger. Pulse until blended and homogenous. Drain to discard fibrous bits.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/chicken-inasal-filipino-chicken-bbq/#wprm-recipe-53235-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/chicken-inasal-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour marinade over chicken wings.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/chicken-inasal-filipino-chicken-bbq/#wprm-recipe-53235-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/chicken-inasal-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer to a ziplock bag and refrigerate for about 2 hours, shaking and turning to evenly distribute marinade every hour.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/chicken-inasal-filipino-chicken-bbq/#wprm-recipe-53235-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/chicken-inasal-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "To make the basting oil, in a saucepan, warm the duck fat then add annatto seeds.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/chicken-inasal-filipino-chicken-bbq/#wprm-recipe-53235-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/chicken-inasal-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "When it begins to bubble, turn off the heat and allow to steep for at least 30 minutes. Strain through a fine-mesh strainer and let cool. Store in an airtight container. May be refrigerated up to two weeks.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/chicken-inasal-filipino-chicken-bbq/#wprm-recipe-53235-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/chicken-inasal-08.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove chicken from the marinade. Lightly grease grill and heat over hot coals. Grill chicken, turning once or twice, basting regularly with annatto oil. Remove from heat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/chicken-inasal-filipino-chicken-bbq/#wprm-recipe-53235-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/chicken-inasal-09.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve with a side of steamed broccoli and spiced vinegar (add crushed garlic, minced shallots, and chopped birds eye chili).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/chicken-inasal-filipino-chicken-bbq/#wprm-recipe-53235-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
